# Repo-root .env is intentionally near-empty.
#
# Each service has its OWN .env file — dotenv is loaded by the service from
# its own working directory, so anything you put here is NOT read by the
# Node services:
#
#   services/api-gateway/.env
#   services/core-service/.env
#   services/insights-service/.env
#   frontend/.env  (Vite — VITE_* vars only)
#   ml/.env        (Python training pipeline)
#
# Copy each `<dir>/.env.example` to `<dir>/.env` and customize. `init.sh`
# does this automatically on first run for any service that has an
# .env.example but no .env yet.

# (No project-wide variables.)
